<urn:atm:triage:finding/AX4-QA-003>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "AX4-QA-003" ;
  triage:title "Duplicate task_state_transition key in .just/lint_boundaries.py IO_FORBIDDEN_SOURCE_PATTERNS: AX.4's unruled addition is dead code shadowed by AX.3's entry" ;
  triage:description "The IO_FORBIDDEN_SOURCE_PATTERNS dict literal (lines 77-251) defines the key task_state_transition twice: AX.4 commit 22833732a added an entry at line 127 with patterns matching no real identifier in the workspace, while AX.3's pre-existing entry at line 236 (from 73a192014) matches the real apply_task_* functions. Python keeps the last literal occurrence, so the AX.4 block is permanently dead and nothing signals which one is live. .just/lint_boundaries.py is a frozen file; this edit had no ruling and fenix does not accept it. Fix (ruled): delete the AX.4-added block at lines 127-130 entirely, restoring the file to the AX.3 content; no other change to the file." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-ax" ;
